# **The precondition, and it is not met on the committed tree.**
# `python3 ec/tools/check_doc_figure_pins.py
# docs/findings/xdata-census-rederivation-checklist.md --section 2b` **exits 1
# today**, and would put the cheap tier red on the commit that lands it: some
# rows §2b marks `held` resolve to no oracle entry, no check literal and no cited
# committed cell, and others cite a `file:line` that measures in a different
# module from the one the row names. That is a real disagreement about
# a published page, and reconciling it is its own piece of work -- which is why
# it is *not* in this patch. Landing first is what makes it cheap: §2b is a
# committed document and the tool names the row and the pin. **Re-measure it at
# the tip you land on**; the disagreement is about text other changes move.
#
# The tool's own verdict vocabulary is what makes that readable rather than
